1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Working memory holds and processes information needed right now. This Chinese psychology definition emphasizes a limited amount of information, maintained for a short time.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Tencent describes agent working memory as remembering where a task stands, and when experience applies. Here, we illustrate the idea using Ravi Bajaj's queue-aware autonomy code.

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Twelve agents exchange state updates. Messages are delayed by three rounds, while each agent can process only two per round. Background traffic competes for those same slots.

4
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:45,000
These replays share the same simulated world. Each agent remembers neighbors through messages. Coral outlines indicate at least one remembered value that disagrees with current reality.

5
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Recent-update priority refreshes that memory faster. Aging reserves a slot for old background work. The moving packets illustrate updates processed in the displayed round.

6
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Across ten matched seeds, memory mismatch falls from about fifty percent with FIFO to twenty-two percent with priority. Aging gives about thirty-four percent.

7
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:10,000
But priority nearly starves background work. All three queues still grow under overload. Freshness and fairness are different objectives.

8
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:22,000
In this basketball example, a queued pass targets a teammate who is now covered. The guard checks current conditions, rejects that pass, and allows a fresh plan to an open teammate.

9
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Two gardening agents remember the same dry plant. The first watering changes its version. The second stale plan is rejected, and repeating the first command cannot add another dose.

10
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Two laundry agents likewise compete for one empty washer. One load is authorized. The other plan is rejected after the state changes. These are executable coordination examples, not robot physics.

11
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:56,000
The existing laundry supervisor goes further. It remembers pending command identity and rejects old observations. Retrying a missing receipt does not trigger another execution.

12
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Even a receipt saying done cannot complete the task. Fresh physical evidence must satisfy the postcondition. We reran all sixteen existing protocol tests successfully.

13
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:18,000
This separate clip comes from the repository's retained humanoid simulation. The robot opens the washer while its receipt is missing. It illustrates the physical application; this video did not rerun the physics.

14
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Useful working memory records state, source, age, and pending action. Assured autonomy checks whether that evidence is still fit to act on. These examples demonstrate mechanisms, not a general safety guarantee.

15
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:40,000
The Chinese definitions, runnable examples, measured traces, and verification results are included with the video. The queue-aware repository is the source of the demonstration.